#: src/reference/recipes/use-sbt-as-metals-build-server.md:1
msgid "Use sbt as Metals build server"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/recipes/use-sbt-as-metals-build-server.md:7
msgid "Objective"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/recipes/use-sbt-as-metals-build-server.md:10
msgid ""
"I want to use [Metals](https://scalameta.org/metals/) on VS Code with sbt as "
"the build server."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/recipes/use-sbt-as-metals-build-server.md:12
msgid "Steps"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/recipes/use-sbt-as-metals-build-server.md:15
msgid "To use Metals on VS Code:"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/recipes/use-sbt-as-metals-build-server.md:17
msgid "Install Metals from Extensions tab:<br> ![Metals](../files/metals0.png)"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/recipes/use-sbt-as-metals-build-server.md:19
msgid "Open a directory containing a `build.sbt` file."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/recipes/use-sbt-as-metals-build-server.md:20
msgid ""
"From the menubar, run View > Command Palette... (`Cmd-Shift-P` on macOS) "
"\"Metals: Switch build server\", and select \"sbt\"<br> ![Metals](../files/"
"metals2.png)"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/recipes/use-sbt-as-metals-build-server.md:22
msgid ""
"Once the import process is complete, open a Scala file to see that code "
"completion works:<br> ![Metals](../files/metals3.png)"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/recipes/use-sbt-as-metals-build-server.md:25
msgid "Use the following setting to opt-out some of the subprojects from BSP."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/recipes/use-sbt-as-metals-build-server.md:31
msgid ""
"When you make changes to the code and save them (`Cmd-S` on macOS), Metals "
"will invoke sbt to do the actual building work."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/recipes/use-sbt-as-metals-build-server.md:34
msgid "Logging into sbt session"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/recipes/use-sbt-as-metals-build-server.md:36
msgid ""
"While Metals uses sbt as the build server, we can also log into the same sbt "
"session using a thin client."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/recipes/use-sbt-as-metals-build-server.md:38
msgid ""
"From Terminal section, type in `sbt --client`<br> ![Metals](../files/"
"metals6.png)"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/recipes/use-sbt-as-metals-build-server.md:41
msgid ""
"This lets you log into the sbt session Metals has started. In there you can "
"call `testOnly` and other tasks with the code already compiled."
msgstr ""
